# Testing & Accessibility

## Component Testing with userEvent

**Always use `@testing-library/user-event` instead of `fireEvent` for user interactions.**

**Key advantages:**

- More realistic user behavior simulation
- Async by default (avoids act() warnings)
- Better accessibility testing
- Proper keyboard navigation support

**Basic pattern:**

```typescript
import userEvent from '@testing-library/user-event'

it('handles user interaction', async () => {
  const user = userEvent.setup()
  render(<Component />)

  await user.click(screen.getByRole('button'))
  await user.type(screen.getByRole('textbox'), 'text')
})
```

**Clean error testing:**

```typescript
// Mock console.error to suppress expected logs
const consoleSpy = vi.spyOn(console, 'error').mockImplementation(() => {})
// ... test error scenarios ...
consoleSpy.mockRestore()
```

## React Testing Library Best Practices (Kent C. Dodds)

**Follow Kent C. Dodds' testing principles: Test your software the way users actually use it.**

### Core Principles

1. **Test behavior, not implementation details**
2. **Use queries that reflect how users interact with your app**
3. **Avoid testing internal state or implementation**
4. **Write tests that give you confidence your app works**

### Query Priority

**Use queries in this order of priority:**

```typescript
// 1. ✅ Accessible to everyone - BEST
screen.getByRole('button', { name: /submit/i })
screen.getByLabelText(/email address/i)

// 2. ✅ Semantic queries - GOOD
screen.getByPlaceholderText(/enter email/i)
screen.getByText(/welcome back/i)
screen.getByDisplayValue(/current value/i)

// 3. ⚠️ Less semantic - USE SPARINGLY
screen.getByAltText(/company logo/i)
screen.getByTitle(/tooltip text/i)

// 4. ❌ Last resort only - AVOID IF POSSIBLE
screen.getByTestId('submit-button')

// ❌ NEVER use these
container.querySelector('.submit-button') // DON'T
container.firstChild // DON'T
```

### Best Practices

#### ✅ DO: Use screen and semantic queries

```typescript
import { render, screen } from '@testing-library/react'
import userEvent from '@testing-library/user-event'

it('allows user to submit form', async () => {
  const user = userEvent.setup()
  const handleSubmit = vi.fn()

  render(<LoginForm onSubmit={handleSubmit} />)

  // Use semantic queries
  await user.type(screen.getByLabelText(/email/i), 'user@example.com')
  await user.type(screen.getByLabelText(/password/i), 'password123')
  await user.click(screen.getByRole('button', { name: /log in/i }))

  expect(handleSubmit).toHaveBeenCalledWith({
    email: 'user@example.com',
    password: 'password123',
  })
})
```

#### ❌ DON'T: Test implementation details

```typescript
// ❌ Bad: Testing internal state
it('updates state on input change', () => {
  const { container } = render(<SearchInput />)
  const input = container.querySelector('input')

  fireEvent.change(input, { target: { value: 'test' } })

  // Don't test internal state
  expect(component.state.searchTerm).toBe('test')
})

// ✅ Good: Test user-visible behavior
it('displays search results when user types', async () => {
  const user = userEvent.setup()
  render(<SearchInput />)

  await user.type(screen.getByRole('searchbox'), 'test query')

  // Test what the user sees
  expect(screen.getByText(/showing results for "test query"/i)).toBeInTheDocument()
})
```

#### ✅ DO: Write longer, more comprehensive tests

```typescript
// ✅ Good: Test complete user flows
it('completes checkout flow', async () => {
  const user = userEvent.setup()
  render(<CheckoutPage />)

  // Fill shipping info
  await user.type(screen.getByLabelText(/name/i), 'John Doe')
  await user.type(screen.getByLabelText(/address/i), '123 Main St')
  await user.click(screen.getByRole('button', { name: /continue/i }))

  // Fill payment info
  await user.type(screen.getByLabelText(/card number/i), '4242424242424242')
  await user.click(screen.getByRole('button', { name: /place order/i }))

  // Verify success
  expect(screen.getByText(/order confirmed/i)).toBeInTheDocument()
})
```

#### ❌ DON'T: Over-mock or use shallow rendering

```typescript
// ❌ Bad: Mocking child components
it('renders user profile', () => {
  vi.mock('./Avatar', () => ({ Avatar: () => <div>Avatar</div> }))
  vi.mock('./UserInfo', () => ({ UserInfo: () => <div>Info</div> }))

  render(<UserProfile />)
  // Tests nothing meaningful
})

// ✅ Good: Render full component tree
it('displays user information', () => {
  const user = { name: 'John Doe', avatar: '/avatar.jpg' }

  render(<UserProfile user={user} />)

  expect(screen.getByText('John Doe')).toBeInTheDocument()
  expect(screen.getByAltText(/john doe/i)).toHaveAttribute('src', '/avatar.jpg')
})
```

#### ✅ DO: Query by role with accessible name

```typescript
// ✅ Good: Query by role and accessible name
it('deletes item when delete button is clicked', async () => {
  const user = userEvent.setup()
  const handleDelete = vi.fn()

  render(<TodoItem title="Buy milk" onDelete={handleDelete} />)

  // Use role with name for specificity
  await user.click(screen.getByRole('button', { name: /delete buy milk/i }))

  expect(handleDelete).toHaveBeenCalled()
})
```

#### ✅ DO: Use waitFor for async behavior

```typescript
// ✅ Good: Wait for async updates
it('loads and displays user data', async () => {
  render(<UserProfile userId="123" />)

  // Show loading state
  expect(screen.getByText(/loading/i)).toBeInTheDocument()

  // Wait for data to load
  expect(await screen.findByText('John Doe')).toBeInTheDocument()

  // Loading state should be gone
  expect(screen.queryByText(/loading/i)).not.toBeInTheDocument()
})
```

#### ❌ DON'T: Use arbitrary waitFor with empty callback

```typescript
// ❌ Bad: Waiting for arbitrary time
await waitFor(() => {})
await new Promise((resolve) => setTimeout(resolve, 1000))

// ✅ Good: Wait for specific condition
await waitFor(() => {
  expect(screen.getByText(/loaded/i)).toBeInTheDocument()
})

// ✅ Better: Use findBy queries (waitFor built-in)
expect(await screen.findByText(/loaded/i)).toBeInTheDocument()
```

### Key Takeaways

- **Use `screen` for queries**: More consistent and easier to read
- **Prefer getByRole**: Most accessible and reliable query
- **Avoid testid**: Only use as last resort when semantic queries aren't possible
- **Test user behavior**: Not implementation details like state or props
- **Use userEvent**: Not fireEvent (already covered above)
- **Write integration tests**: Test components working together, not in isolation
- **Avoid shallow rendering**: Render the full component tree

